# The `.claude/` capability layer IS this repo — skills, hooks, agents,
# registries and capability routing are all tracked. A blanket `.claude` rule
# lived here until 2026-07-31 and silently excluded every one of them; do not
# reintroduce it. Ignore individual machine-local paths below instead.

# Hook run logs. The hooks are stateless as of 2026-08-03 and nothing writes one
# any more -- `_hooklib.write_log` is gone, and twelve files had accumulated of
# which ten had no writer at all. This rule is kept as a standing guard, not as
# live bookkeeping: the entries captured prompt text and transcript paths
# verbatim, and that reaching git history is not something you undo. One line to
# keep, so keeping it is cheaper than the failure it prevents.
.claude/hooks/*.log

# Machine-local: which project MCP servers this machine has approved.
# Belongs to the checkout, not the repo.
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Hook state: per-turn and per-review bookkeeping, rewritten constantly and
# meaningful only to this checkout. Tracking it churns every commit.
#
# Two reasons, one of them now historical. `05-docs-gate.py` (DELETED
# 2026-08-02) counted changed files that were not knowledge docs, so a tracked
# marker made that gate partly trigger on its own bookkeeping. The live reason
# is `review-receipts.json`: tracked until 2026-08-02, and its writes changed
# the fingerprint it had just recorded, so no receipt ever survived. See
# ISSUES.md 2026-08-01 21:15.
.claude/hooks/state/
.claude/workflow-state/
node_modules/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
